attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13995396/state.json" "file_sha256" "a8d28256e6803c2971008e602f20171bc19959935817df7f8326a48befe04d62" "basis" 1061 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13995396/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "e-4518" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "The system of equations\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\begin{aligned}6x+4y=1 \\\\ x-8y-z=-2 \\\\ 3x+2y-2z=1\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\ncan be represented using matrix notation as\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}a & 4 & 0 \\\\ 1 & -8 & -1 \\\\ 3 & b & -2\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nWhat are the values of $a,$ $b$ and $c?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13995396/example-4518.json" "file_sha256" "18e68fafb8b2de1af96577a6bcd8efa08b752c29b391e9577282a7f36f5c1aba" "basis" 1061 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13995396/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "e-4518" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, let's write the system so that $x$, $y$, and $z$ appear in each equation:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}6x+4y+0z=1 \\\\ x-8y-z=-2 \\\\ 3x+2y-2z=1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can write the system in the form $A\\mathbf{x} = \\mathbf{b},$ where\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}6 & 4 & 0 \\\\ 1 & -8 & -1 \\\\ 3 & 2 & -2\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nis the coefficient matrix,\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nis the column vector of constants, and\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nis the column vector of variables.\n\nSo, the equation $A\\mathbf{x} = \\mathbf{b}$ becomes\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}6 & 4 & 0 \\\\ 1 & -8 & -1 \\\\ 3 & 2 & -2\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nTherefore, $a=6,$ $b=2,$ and $c=-2.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13995396/example-4518.json" "file_sha256" "18e68fafb8b2de1af96577a6bcd8efa08b752c29b391e9577282a7f36f5c1aba" "basis" 1061 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13995396/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "e-4519" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "The system of equations\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\begin{aligned}2x-y+z=4 \\\\ z-x+2=-1 \\\\ 2y-2x-4z=-4\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\ncan be represented using matrix notation as\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 & 1 \\\\ -1 & a & 1 \\\\ b & 2 & -4\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nWhat are the values of $a,$ $b$ and $c?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13995396/example-4519.json" "file_sha256" "00a9c6203c8116ac89df8de2ccc1d12b50bb067c9df5d3e5f10ca42b2535a35f" "basis" 1061 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13995396/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "e-4519" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, let's write the system so that $x$, $y$, and $z$ appear in each equation in the correct order and all constants are on the right-hand side of the system:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}2x-y+z=4 \\\\ -x+0y+z=-3 \\\\ -2x+2y-4z=-4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can write the system in the form $A\\mathbf{x} = \\mathbf{b},$ where\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 0 & 1 \\\\ -2 & 2 & -4\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nis the coefficient matrix,\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ -3 \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nis the column vector of constants, and\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nis the column vector of variables.\n\nSo, the equation $A\\mathbf{x} = \\mathbf{b}$ becomes\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 0 & 1 \\\\ -2 & 2 & -4\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nTherefore $a=0,$ $b=-2,$ $c=-3.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13995396/example-4519.json" "file_sha256" "00a9c6203c8116ac89df8de2ccc1d12b50bb067c9df5d3e5f10ca42b2535a35f" "basis" 1061 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13995396/edb-import/verification.json"}] "sources" [{"question" "q-130536" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "The system of equations\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}-3x+y+7z=5 \\\\ x-4y+8z=1 \\\\ -6y+9z=2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\ncan be represented using matrix notation as\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 1 & 7 \\\\ 1 & -4 & b \\\\ 0 & a & 9\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}c \\\\ 1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nWhat are the values of $a,b,$ and $c?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14052721/state.json" "file_sha256" "46ea079729a5544ab3430644feb74dedfb6a81f2354bbf2561fc13dc58abe0aa"} {"question" "q-130536" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, let's write the system so that $x$, $y$, and $z$ appear in each equation:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}-3x+y+7z=5 \\\\ x-4y+8z=1 \\\\ 0x-6y+9z=2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can write the system in the form $Ax=b,$ where\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 1 & 7 \\\\ 1 & -4 & 8 \\\\ 0 & -6 & 9\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nis the coefficient matrix,\n\n$$\nb=[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nis the column vector of constants, and\n\n$$\nx=[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nis the column vector of variables.\n\nSo, the equation $Ax=b$ becomes\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 1 & 7 \\\\ 1 & -4 & 8 \\\\ 0 & -6 & 9\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTherefore, $a=-6,\\,b=8,\\,c=5.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14052721/state.json" "file_sha256" "46ea079729a5544ab3430644feb74dedfb6a81f2354bbf2561fc13dc58abe0aa"} {"question" "q-130536" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14052721/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "ba9737e7eae048ec45c4a9960d0262eb7db37b4e9e9c5d74a8d439d7acc31b68"} {"question" "q-130536" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14052721/state.json" "file_sha256" "46ea079729a5544ab3430644feb74dedfb6a81f2354bbf2561fc13dc58abe0aa"} {"question" "q-130536" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "a=-3,\\,b=1,\\,c=2"] ["math" "a=-4,\\,b=8,\\,c=-3"] ["math" "a=-6,\\,b=8,\\,c=5"] ["math" "a=0,\\,b=8,\\,c=1"] ["math" "a=1,\\,b=7,\\,c=8"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14052721/state.json" "file_sha256" "46ea079729a5544ab3430644feb74dedfb6a81f2354bbf2561fc13dc58abe0aa"} {"question" "q-130536" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "a=-6,\\,b=8,\\,c=5"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14052721/state.json" "file_sha256" "46ea079729a5544ab3430644feb74dedfb6a81f2354bbf2561fc13dc58abe0aa"} {"question" "q-36181" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "The system of equations\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}3x-4y+z=2 \\\\ x-6y+11z=3 \\\\ 3x-4y-z=4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\ncan be represented using matrix notation as\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}3 & -4 & a \\\\ 1 & b & c \\\\ 3 & -4 & -1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nWhat are the values of $a,b$ and $c?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14052721/state.json" "file_sha256" "46ea079729a5544ab3430644feb74dedfb6a81f2354bbf2561fc13dc58abe0aa"} {"question" "q-36181" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We can write the system in the form $Ax=b,$ where\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}3 & -4 & 1 \\\\ 1 & -6 & 11 \\\\ 3 & -4 & -1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nis the coefficient matrix,\n\n$$\nb=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nis the column vector of constants, and\n\n$$\nx=[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nis the column vector of variables.\n\nSo, the equation $Ax=b$ becomes\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}3 & -4 & 1 \\\\ 1 & -6 & 11 \\\\ 3 & -4 & -1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTherefore, $a=1,\\,b=-6,\\,c=11.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14052721/state.json" "file_sha256" "46ea079729a5544ab3430644feb74dedfb6a81f2354bbf2561fc13dc58abe0aa"} {"question" "q-36181" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14052721/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "ba9737e7eae048ec45c4a9960d0262eb7db37b4e9e9c5d74a8d439d7acc31b68"} {"question" "q-36181" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14052721/state.json" "file_sha256" "46ea079729a5544ab3430644feb74dedfb6a81f2354bbf2561fc13dc58abe0aa"} {"question" "q-36181" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answe