 \\\\ 4 & -7 & -1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTherefore, $a=4,\\,b=-3,\\,c=1.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14052721/state.json" "file_sha256" "46ea079729a5544ab3430644feb74dedfb6a81f2354bbf2561fc13dc58abe0aa"} {"question" "q-130535" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14052721/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "ba9737e7eae048ec45c4a9960d0262eb7db37b4e9e9c5d74a8d439d7acc31b68"} {"question" "q-130535" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14052721/state.json" "file_sha256" "46ea079729a5544ab3430644feb74dedfb6a81f2354bbf2561fc13dc58abe0aa"} {"question" "q-130535" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "a=-1,\\,b=-5,\\,c=9"] ["math" "a=2,\\,b=-3,\\,c=1"] ["math" "a=2,\\,b=-7,\\,c=-1"] ["math" "a=4,\\,b=-1,\\,c=1"] ["math" "a=4,\\,b=-3,\\,c=1"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14052721/state.json" "file_sha256" "46ea079729a5544ab3430644feb74dedfb6a81f2354bbf2561fc13dc58abe0aa"} {"question" "q-130535" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "a=4,\\,b=-3,\\,c=1"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14052721/state.json" "file_sha256" "46ea079729a5544ab3430644feb74dedfb6a81f2354bbf2561fc13dc58abe0aa"} {"question" "q-316977" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "The system of equations\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x-y+z=11 \\\\ -x-3y-z=0 \\\\ 8x+6y+3z=-9\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\ncan be represented using matrix notation as\n\n|  |  | $1$ | $-1$ | {{field-1}} |  |  |  | $x$ |  |  |  | {{field-2}} |  |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  |  | $-1$ | {{field-3}} | $-1$ |  |  |  | $y$ |  | $=$ |  | $0$ |  | . |\n|  |  | {{field-4}} | $6$ | $3$ |  |  |  | $z$ |  |  |  | $-9$ |  |  |" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14052721/state.json" "file_sha256" "46ea079729a5544ab3430644feb74dedfb6a81f2354bbf2561fc13dc58abe0aa"} {"question" "q-316977" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, let's write the system so that $x$, $y$, and $z$ appear in each equation:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x-y+z=11 \\\\ -x-3y-z=0 \\\\ 8x+6y+3z=-9\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can write the system in the form $Ax=b,$ where\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & 1 \\\\ -1 & -3 & -1 \\\\ 8 & 6 & 3\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nis the coefficient matrix,\n\n$$\nb=[\\begin{aligned}11 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -9\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nis the column vector of constants, and\n\n$$\nx=[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nis the column vector of variables.\n\nSo, the equation $Ax=b$ becomes\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & 1 \\\\ -1 & -3 & -1 \\\\ 8 & 6 & 3\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}11 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -9\\end{aligned}].\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14052721/state.json" "file_sha256" "46ea079729a5544ab3430644feb74dedfb6a81f2354bbf2561fc13dc58abe0aa"} {"question" "q-316977" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14052721/activity-m