igned}][\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}a \\\\ 3 \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nWhat are the values of $a,b$ and $c?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14052721/state.json" "file_sha256" "46ea079729a5544ab3430644feb74dedfb6a81f2354bbf2561fc13dc58abe0aa"} {"question" "q-75511" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, let's write the system so that $x$, $y$, and $z$ appear in each equation in the correct order and all constants are on the right-hand side of the system:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\begin{aligned}-2x+y+z=-1 \\\\ 3x-2y+z=3 \\\\ -x-y+2z=-4\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can write the system in the form $Ax=b,$ where\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 3 & -2 & 1 \\\\ -1 & -1 & 2\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nis the coefficient matrix,\n\n$$\nb=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 3 \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nis the column vector of constants, and\n\n$$\nx=[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nis the column vector of variables.\n\nSo, the equation $Ax=b$ becomes\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 3 & -2 & 1 \\\\ -1 & -1 & 2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 3 \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTherefore, $a=-1,\\,b=-2,\\,c=2.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14052721/state.json" "file_sha256" "46ea079729a5544ab3430644feb74dedfb6a81f2354bbf2561fc13dc58abe0aa"} {"question" "q-75511" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14052721/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "ba9737e7eae048ec45c4a9960d0262eb7db37b4e9e9c5d74a8d439d7acc31b68"} {"question" "q-75511" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answe