der and all constants are on the right-hand side of the system:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\begin{aligned}-7x+0y+z=5 \\\\ -x+4y-3z=2 \\\\ x+2y+0z=6\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can write the system in the form $Ax=b,$ where\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}-7 & 0 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 4 & -3 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 0\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nis the coefficient matrix,\n\n$$\nb=[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nis the column vector of constants, and\n\n$$\nx=[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nis the column vector of variables.\n\nSo, the equation $Ax=b$ becomes\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}7 & 0 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 4 & -3 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 0\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTherefore, $a=-3,\\,b=1,\\,c=6.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14052721/state.json" "file_sha256" "46ea079729a5544ab3430644feb74dedfb6a81f2354bbf2561fc13dc58abe0aa"} {"question" "q-130562" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14052721/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "ba9737e7eae048ec45c4a9960d0262eb7db37b4e9e9c5d74a8d439d7acc31b68"} {"question" "q-130562" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14052721/state.json" "file_sha256" "46ea079729a5544ab3430644feb74dedfb6a81f2354bbf2561fc13dc58abe0aa"} {"question" "q-130562" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "a=-3,\\,b=1,\\,c=6"] ["math" "a=-3,\\,b=5,\\,c=8"] ["math" "a=-7,\\,b=1,\\,c=1"] ["math" "a=1,\\,b=-7,\\,c=8"] ["math" "a=4,\\,b=1,\\,c=0"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14052721/state.json" "file_sha256" "46ea079729a5544ab3430644feb74dedfb6a81f2354bbf2561fc13dc58abe0aa"} {"question" "q-130562" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "a=-3,\\,b=1,\\,c=6"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14052721/state.json" "file_sha256" "46ea079729a5544ab3430644feb74dedfb6a81f2354bbf2561fc13dc58abe0aa"} {"question" "q-75501" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "The system of equations\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\begin{aligned}5y-3z+x=2 \\\\ 3z+7x-2y=5 \\\\ 2x-2y=-1\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\ncan be represented using matrix notation as\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}a & 5 & -3 \\\\ 7 & b & 3 \\\\ 2 & -2 & c\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 5 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nWhat are the values of $a,b$ and $c?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14052721/state.json" "file_sha256" "46ea079729a5544ab3430644feb74dedfb6a81f2354bbf2561fc13dc58abe0aa"} {"question" "q-75501" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, let's write the system so that $x$, $y$, and $z$ appear in each equation in the correct order and all constants are on the right-hand side of the system:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\begin{aligned}x+5y-3z=2 \\\\ 7x-2y+3z=5 \\\\ 2x-2y+0z=-1\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can write the system in the form $Ax=b,$ where\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 5 & -3 \\\\ 7 & -2 & 3 \\\\ 2 & -2 & 0\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nis the coefficient matrix,\n\n$$\nb=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 5 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nis the column vector of constants, and\n\n$$\nx=[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nis the column vector of variables.\n\nSo, the equation $Ax=b$ becomes\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}1 & 5 & -3 \\\\ 7 & -2 & 3 \\\\ 2 & -2 & 0\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 5 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTherefore, $a=1,\\,b=-2,\\,c=0.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14052721/state.json" "file_sha256" "46ea079729a5544ab3430644feb74dedfb6a81f2354bbf2561fc13dc58abe0aa"} {"question" "q-75501" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14052721/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "ba9737e7eae048ec45c4a9960d0262eb7db37b4e9e9c5d74a8d439d7acc31b68"} {"question" "q-75501" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14052721/state.json" "file_sha256" "46ea079729a5544ab3430644feb74dedfb6a81f2354bbf2561fc13dc58abe0aa"} {"question" "q-75501" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "a=1,\\,b=-2,\\,c=0"] ["math" "a=1,\\,b=-2,\\,c=1"] ["math" "a=1,\\,b=7,\\,c=0"] ["math" "a=5,\\,b=7,\\,c=0"] ["math" "a=5,\\,b=7,\\,c=1"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14052721/state.json" "file_sha256" "46ea079729a5544ab3430644feb74dedfb6a81f2354bbf2561fc13dc58abe0aa"} {"question" "q-75501" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "a=1,\\,b=-2,\\,c=0"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14052721/state.json" "file_sha256" "46ea079729a5544ab3430644feb74dedfb6a81f2354bbf2561fc13dc58abe0aa"} {"question" "q-75490" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "The system of equations\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\begin{aligned}2y+5x=3z+2 \\\\ 3x-6y=5 \\\\ 2x-3y+5z=-1\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\ncan be represented using matrix notation as\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}5 & a & -3 \\\\ 3 & -6 & b \\\\ 2 & c & 5\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 5 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nWhat are the values of $a,b$ and $c?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14052721/state.json" "file_sha256" "46ea079729a5544ab3430644feb74dedfb6a81f2354bbf2561fc13dc58abe0aa"} {"question" "q-75490" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, let's write the system so that $x$, $y$, and $z$ appear in each equation in the correct order and all constants are on the right-hand side of the system:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\begin{aligned}5x+2y-3z=2 \\\\ 3x-6y+0z=5 \\\\ 2x-3y+5z=-1\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can write the system in the form $Ax=b,$ where\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}5 & 2 & -3 \\\\ 3 & -6 & 0 \\\\ 2 & -3 & 5\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nis the coefficient matrix,\n\n$$\nb=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 5 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nis the column vector of constants, and\n\n$$\nx=[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nis the column vector of variables.\n\nSo, the equation $Ax=b$ becomes\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}5 & 2 & -3 \\\\ 3 & -6 & 0 \\\\ 2 & -3 & 5\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 5 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTherefore, $a=2,\\,b=0,\\,c=-3.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14052721/state.json" "file_sha256" "46ea079729a5544ab3430644feb74dedfb6a81f2354bbf2561fc13dc58abe0aa"} {"question" "q-75490" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14052721/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "ba9737e7eae048ec45c4a9960d0262eb7db37b4e9e9c5d74a8d439d7acc31b68"} {"question" "q-75490" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14052721/state.json" "file_sha256" "46ea079729a5544ab3430644feb74dedfb6a81f2354bbf2561fc13dc58abe0aa"} {"question" "q-75490" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "a=-3,\\,b=0,\\,c=-3"] ["math" "a=2,\\,b=-6,\\,c=-3"] ["math" "a=2,\\,b=0,\\,c=-3"] ["math" "a=2,\\,b=1,\\,c=-1"] ["math" "a=5,\\,b=-6,\\,c=-1"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14052721/state.json" "file_sha256" "46ea079729a5544ab3430644feb74dedfb6a81f2354bbf2561fc13dc58abe0aa"} {"question" "q-75490" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "a=2,\\,b=0,\\,c=-3"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14052721/state.json" "file_sha256" "46ea079729a5544ab3430644feb74dedfb6a81f2354bbf2561fc13dc58abe0aa"} {"question" "q-75512" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "The system of equations\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\begin{aligned}-2z+x-5y=1 \\\\ -y+5z-4x=-2 \\\\ 2x-6y-z=2\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\ncan be represented using matrix notation as\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}1 & -5 & a \\\\ b & -1 & 5 \\\\ 2 & c & -1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nWhat are the values of $a,b$ and $c?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14052721/state.json" "file_sha256" "46ea079729a5544ab3430644feb74dedfb6a81f2354bbf2561fc13dc58abe0aa"} {"question" "q-75512" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, let's write the system so that $x$, $y$, and $z$ appear in each equation in the correct order and all constants are on the right-hand side of the system:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\begin{aligned}x-5y-2z=1 \\\\ -4x-y+5z=-2 \\\\ 2x-6y-z=2\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can write the system in the form $Ax=b,$ where\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -5 & -2 \\\\ -4 & -1 & 5 \\\\ 2 & -6 & -1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nis the coefficient matrix,\n\n$$\nb=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nis the column vector of constants, and\n\n$$\nx=[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nis the column vector of variables.\n\nSo, the equation $Ax=b$ becomes\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}1 & -5 & -2 \\\\ -4 & -1 & 5 \\\\ 2 & -6 & -1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTherefore, $a=-2,\\,b=-4,\\,c=-6.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14052721/state.json" "file_sha256" "46ea079729a5544ab3430644feb74dedfb6a81f2354bbf2561fc13dc58abe0aa"} {"question" "q-75512" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14052721/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "ba9737e7eae048ec45c4a9960d0262eb7db37b4e9e9c5d74a8d439d7acc31b68"} {"question" "q-75512" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14052721/state.json" "file_sha256" "46ea079729a5544ab3430644feb74dedfb6a81f2354bbf2561fc13dc5